Having a redundant load balancer setup is essential to ensure high availability and minimize downtime. Whether you choose an active-passive or active-active configuration, or opt for a cloud-managed service, the key is to have a well-tested failover mechanism in place. This will help you maintain service continuity even if the primary load balancer fails.

